handoff:
  - "Design: capture contract. captureBookStill returns { color, lineArt, camera, warnings? } from one page load: it starts a vite dev server (localhost, plugins serve only out/ and the stage directory), launches Chromium, loads song.html, waits for window.__song.ready, loads the book timeline with window.__song.load, asserts empty page notes, seeks to the stage still time with window.__song.seek, and screenshots the color twin. playwright and vite load lazily inside the capture function only. A plain Buffer return (the pre-line-art draft shape) is accepted for cover and small jobs and refused for reader pages, so a reader page can never get a lone color file."
  - "Design: line-art pass. The line art is a render pass of the same three.js scene inside the page: a second render of the same scene and camera through a WebGLRenderTarget with a black wireframe override material on a white background, read back with readRenderTargetPixels, thresholded to 0/255, row-flipped, and packed to one grey channel. The technique is versioned as lineArtTechnique 'song-page-scene-render-pass-1bit-v1' with lineArtFormatVersion 'storytime-lineart-provisional-v1'. It is NOT a filter of the color PNG."
  - "BLOCKER for the live pass (strategy section 8): src/song/main.ts exposes only window.__song with ready, portrait, load, seek. The scene, camera, and renderer are module-scoped and unreachable, so captureBookStill throws a precise error until an engine hook exists. The needed change is small: after seek, set window.__bookStill = { scene, camera, renderer, cameraState } (cameraState = position, target, fov after the seek). Per the contract that change gets its own task, tests/song-timeline.test.ts in its gate, and a PM note. The orchestrator should add that engine-hook task before Phase 3 task 1 (Nan window sample). git diff --quiet 1d39b8fda457e12d8e7332e7de65d2046ddda78e -- src/song still exits 0; src/song was not edited."
  - "Design: twin binding and checks. One render run writes color file, line-art file (under <directory>/lineart/), and one evidence record with one stage hash, one still time, one camera, and both file hashes. Render-time validation covers the color PNG and the line-art format before any write, so a failure in either pass writes neither twin. Manifest line-art readiness needs: format checks valid, binding intact (competing per-twin fields in the evidence fail it), a ready color twin, a passing line-art person look, and the style look reviews/lineart-style-look.json with evidenceClass owner-passed. verify --release requires the ready twin for reader pages; --output color and --output lineart limit the selection and an empty selection fails."
  - "Design: heavy rule. scripts/storytime-book-pictures.ts now delegates real render runs to the PM's one command (bash ~/Desktop/advantage-pr/scripts/jobs/heavy-run.sh -c '<inner run>') with an inner-run marker that prevents recursion. Injected dependencies keep the preflight, lock, pipeline order that T11 proves. Exit 75 from heavy-run means the preflight hold outlasted the wait; retry up to three times."
  - "Residual risks. (1) The wireframe pass technique is unproven on a real render; the Nan sample is its first live proof, and the limits (90 percent edge whiteness, 0.5 to 25 percent ink) are provisional. A dense wireframe may exceed the ink limit; if Daniel rejects the look, introduce a new technique version. (2) The cover calm-region check compares the top 30 percent against its dominant colour bucket with a 2 percent focal share; a real cover with a graded sky should pass, but the first real cover render needs a look. (3) The render-time line-art validation makes an all-white or oversized line-art pass fail the whole run (atomic), which is correct but means the pass must be tuned before Phase 3 volume. (4) The Kimi review model name is declared ('kimi-k3.1-pro'), not provider-reported; the price note records that."
